    "turn_text": "Not everybody. Some don't have a sense of humor, but grassy. So I get in the subway that goes from the capitol to the heart building and Chuck's sitting right across to me and he goes, oh, you look just like you look on TV. And I said, well, there's a reason for that. I said, but actually, you know, some people say that I'm shorter than I look on TV and he goes, oh yeah, well guess what they say about me? And I said that you're taller than you look on TV. He goes, yeah, had you all that? And I said, well, because you're taller than you look on TV. And I said, well, guess what else they see about me? That you're a friendlier than you seem on TV. Yeah, how did you know that? And I said, well, because you're friendlier than you seem on TV. I said, you know, it wouldn't hurt when you do an interview to smile every once in a while. I said, well, normally what I am talking about is pretty serious. And I saw it don't smile. And I said, well, you could smile at the beginning. And talk about the serious stuff and then smile at the end. Oh, that's a good idea.",
