    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/8/48777.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 110,
    "turn_text": "You know, we were, one of the tragedies, I don't know if it's tragic yet of this new iteration of Trumpcare, is that we were doing a bipartisan, we were having bipartisan hearings in the health committee, health education, labor and pension committees, to shore up the exchanges and lower the costs of them. We knew how to do it. And we had five, yes, I mean we had five, The first day hearings, we had five insurance commissioners, three Republican states, two Democrats. All five agreed that we should continue to cost sharing and we should do reinsurance. And I won't explain these because I don't want you to get angry at me for boring you. But they're really important. And then we had five governors the next day, and three from Republican states, two from Democratic states. And they all agreed on this stuff. And then we had, next week we had two hearings as well. And not only that, but we had coffees. We had these hearings that at 10 in the morning, but at 9 we had a coffee so that everybody, every other senator wasn't on the committee could ask questions. And so we had like half the Senate with these people. This is how you're supposed to do things. And we were doing it. And we were Lamar Alexander the Chairman and Patty Murray the ranking member were negotiating and Lamar said to Patty that all that's that's a good offer the last and then bum McConnell",
