        "text": "The opposing party has failed to meet Democratic standards or expectations on key issues.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Democratic unity and ideological purity are more important than bipartisan cooperation.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The current political environment justifies rejecting compromise as a viable strategy.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "It is reasonable to expect the opposing party to change its views rather than engage in mutual adjustment.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "This hardline stance reflects a broader trend within the Democratic Party today.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Assert / Elaborate"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 48777,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/8/48777.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 156,
    "turn_text": "And in fact, well, it isn't necessarily halfway, but, you know, and a lot of things aren't just, they can't be just about halfway.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
