    "turn_text": "Well, it's your future. You know, we've had these super storms lately and there's no question that they're The effect of their destructive effect has been increased by global warming. We can't tie any one weather event to climate change, but we know that with sea level rising and with it being warmer and the atmosphere being warmer, that it holds more rain. And so that's part of what happened in Houston. You know, climate change is something that if you're in high school, you know, I have grandchildren now. I have three grandchildren. And I don't want them in 50 years saying to me, grandpa, you know, you're a member of the United States Senate. You knew climate change was happening. Why didn't you do anything about it? And also why are you still alive?",
